coreboot -> UefiPayloadPkg -> UEFI Shell, booted inside the patched VirtualBox
(OVH, Debian trixie, 2026-10-21). COM1 serial capture, tail.

coreboot hands off to the payload:

  CBFS: Found 'fallback/payload' @0x1bb00 size 0x15f5e7 in mcache @0x7fffeb90
  Loading Segment: addr: 0x00800000 memsz: 0x0000000000a00000 filesz: 0x000000000015f5af
  using LZMA
    Entry Point 0x00802262
  BS: BS_PAYLOAD_LOAD run times (exec / console): 78 / 3 ms
  Jumping to boot code at 0x00802262(0x7fe9c000)

UefiPayloadPkg runs DXE + BDS and drops to the interactive shell:

    F2 or Down      to enter Setup Option Menu.
    ENTER           to boot directly.
  UEFI Interactive Shell v2.2
  EDK II
  UEFI v2.70 (EDK II, 0x00010000)
  Welcome to the UEFI Shell!
  If you wound up here by mistake, just type 'exit' to return to the UEFI Options Menu.
  Shell>

Functional ACPI, confirmed end to end: issuing `reset -s` at the Shell prompt
(an ACPI S5 shutdown: SLP_TYP=5 written WITH SLP_EN) powers the VM off cleanly --
  Shell> reset -s
  VBox.log: ACPI: Entering S5 power state (power down)
  (VM transitions to OFF on its own)
while coreboot's harmless boot-time SLP_TYP=5 write with SLP_EN clear is correctly
ignored by the DevACPI SLP_EN fix.
